  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe ring-link law of PR #3818 reaches a 2D Pocket with Outside containment. The lines are `crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket.rs:351-354`, `ring_links.rs:88` and `level_order.rs:106`.\n\nThe PR body says \"2D Pocket Outside does not change\". The code takes the new law for that case.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe review found the case is safe: every chord must clear the certified cutter-centre area, which keeps the tool centre one tool radius from the part. But no test pins the Pocket Outside case. A later change can break it with no red test.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd a pin for a 2D Pocket with Outside containment. Assert the link moves and the `link:` notes. Then correct the PR body or the decision file `docs/decisions/3747-in-plane-ring-links.md` to say that this case takes the law.\n\n## Scope\n\nFound in the review of #3818 at head `968fa46d7`. The case is safe today.\n",
